  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA low pressure system approaches from the west, entering the \nMiddle Ohio Valley this weekend. Showers and thunderstorms are \nexpected to move into the western half of the forecast area on \nSaturday, then spread east as the system pivots overhead \nSaturday night into Sunday.\n\nPrecipitable water values ranging from 1.5 to nearly 2.25 inches \nsignal potential for heavy downpours to accompany any showers or \nstorms that develop this weekend. These heavy downpours could\nlead to localized flash flooding, particularly in poor \ndrainage areas.\n\nModel soundings also project a favorable environment for some \nstronger storms to develop amid moderate instability, plenty of \nmoisture, and 30 to 40 kts of shear Sunday afternoon.\nInstability should then taper off after sundown.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nSome model solutions ferry the weekend system off to the \nnortheast before pulling another low up into the area from the \nGulf states. Another potential scenario involves a cutoff low \ndeveloping over the area and then lingering through the majority\nof the work week. While details are yet uncertain, either \nscenario should support chances of at least diurnally driven \nshowers and thunderstorms through much of the work week.",
